# Contributing

## Environment

Use Python 3.11 or newer and uv. Dependencies are declared in
`pyproject.toml`; install them with `uv sync --locked` (or `uv sync`).

## Checks to run before submitting

- Format and lint: `uv run ruff check .`
- Type checks: `uv run mypy src`
- Tests: `uv run pytest -q`
- Build: `uv build`

Run the full suite, not just changed tests, and keep the generated
`uv.lock` in sync when touching dependencies. When you change
distribution or packaging code, also run the package and installer
tests: `uv run pytest tests/test_distribution_policy.py tests/test_installer.py -q`.

## What not to add

- No MCP server or MCP configuration; no runtime Node, CDN assets, or
  extra graph formats.
- No shell interpolation in subprocesses and no `0.0.0.0` binds; the
  viz server is loopback-only.
- No generated wiki content as canonical input; canonical Markdown notes
  are authoritative, SQLite is derived and disposable.

## Releasing

Every release is gated on a live benchmark run: the fixed corpus and
tasks must be measured through the configured harnesses, and any absent
or `NOT_MEASURED` required cell blocks the release. See the benchmark
notes under `bench/` and the CI/release workflows under `.github/`.
